.elixir_ls/

# Regenerated on every `mix ex_tauri.dev`. In dev it is a shell shim holding this
# machine's absolute project path; in a production build it is a Burrito binary.
/burrito_out

# Build output from tailwind + esbuild (`mix assets.build`). The genuinely-source
# assets next to these — favicon.ico, images/, robots.txt — stay tracked.
# The :desktop release prepends a build_assets/1 step so an assembled release
# still gets them (see mix.exs); :assemble alone only copies priv/static.
/priv/static/assets/

# Digest cache written by `phx.digest` during `mix assets.deploy`.
/priv/static/cache_manifest.json

# The rest of what `phx.digest` emits: a content-hashed copy of every file in
# priv/static, plus gzipped variants. Build output, same as the assets/ directory
# above — but not covered by it, because these land beside the sources they were
# made from (favicon-<hash>.ico next to favicon.ico).
#
# The 32 `?` match the digest's hash exactly, rather than the tempting
# `/priv/static/*-*.*`, which would also silently swallow any future source file
# with a hyphen in its name.
/priv/static/*-????????????????????????????????.*
/priv/static/*.gz

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, task briefs, implementer reports and
# review packages for in-flight plans. Regenerable coordination state, not source.
/.superpowers/
